Eee!

268
00:16:27,611 --> 00:16:28,171
Eee!

269
00:16:28,171 --> 00:16:28,251
Eee!

270
00:16:28,251 --> 00:16:28,811
Eee!

271
00:16:28,811 --> 00:16:29,371
Eee!

272
00:16:30,891 --> 00:16:31,451
Gah!

273
00:16:31,451 --> 00:16:33,931
Chomper, that's not a giraffe!

274
00:16:33,931 --> 00:16:36,011
That's a horse with a long neck!

275
00:16:36,011 --> 00:16:37,051
A long horse!

276
00:16:37,051 --> 00:16:38,011
You're a horse?

277
00:16:38,011 --> 00:16:38,731
Eee!

278
00:16:38,731 --> 00:16:39,451
Eee!

279
00:16:39,451 --> 00:16:41,531
Wow, what a pretty horse!

280
00:16:41,531 --> 00:16:42,091
Eee!

281
00:16:42,091 --> 00:16:43,211
Eee!

282
00:16:43,211 --> 00:16:45,451
She said thank you, and her name's Shelly!

283
00:16:45,451 --> 00:16:48,811
Going by the saddle she's got on her, her owner must be close by.

284
00:16:48,811 --> 00:16:49,851
Huh?

285
00:16:50,571 --> 00:16:51,851
Hey, what are you looking at?

286
00:16:52,891 --> 00:16:53,851
Over there.

287
00:16:53,851 --> 00:16:56,171
There's something up with those two bamboo trees.

288
00:16:56,171 --> 00:16:56,891
Huh?

289
00:16:58,011 --> 00:16:58,891
Yeah, you're right!

290
00:16:58,891 --> 00:17:00,251
Talk about tall!

291
00:17:00,251 --> 00:17:01,611
I can't even see the top!

292
00:17:02,171 --> 00:17:03,051
That's not it.

293
00:17:03,051 --> 00:17:03,931
Look closer.

294
00:17:04,491 --> 00:17:05,211
Huh?

295
00:17:05,211 --> 00:17:06,091
Uh...

296
00:17:06,091 --> 00:17:07,291
Gah!

297
00:17:07,291 --> 00:17:08,011
They're moving!

298
00:17:09,771 --> 00:17:11,691
They must be part of some long animal!

299
00:17:13,131 --> 00:17:15,531
That thing's attacking Luffy!

300
00:17:15,531 --> 00:17:16,331
Are you okay?

301
00:17:16,331 --> 00:17:19,771
Get back here, bamboo!

302
00:17:19,771 --> 00:17:21,371
Be careful, Luffy!

303
00:17:21,371 --> 00:17:22,891
Bum, bum!

304
00:17:30,091 --> 00:17:31,051
All right!

305
00:17:31,051 --> 00:17:31,851
You did it!

306
00:17:31,851 --> 00:17:32,971
Yeah!

307
00:17:32,971 --> 00:17:34,331
I beat it!

308
00:17:34,331 --> 00:17:35,371
Why are you alone?

309
00:17:35,371 --> 00:17:36,331
Where's your owner?

310
00:17:38,011 --> 00:17:39,131
You don't know where?

311
00:17:40,011 --> 00:17:41,691
That sounds awfully lonely.

312
00:17:46,331 --> 00:17:49,531
It might be bad guys!

313
00:17:49,531 --> 00:17:50,411
Stay there!

314
00:17:50,411 --> 00:17:50,971
And hide!

315
00:17:52,171 --> 00:17:53,211
What's going on?

316
00:17:55,051 --> 00:17:55,691
Well, uh...

317
00:17:57,371 --> 00:18:00,571
I think that bamboo tree was possessed by this spirit.

318
00:18:12,731 --> 00:18:14,011
Hey, what's the deal?

319
00:18:14,011 --> 00:18:15,131
They blocked in our ship.

320
00:18:16,251 --> 00:18:17,291
This can't be good.

321
00:18:18,251 --> 00:18:19,771
That's the ship I saw earlier.

322
00:18:21,131 --> 00:18:22,411
You looking for a fight?

323
00:18:23,291 --> 00:18:25,131
Because we'll be happy to give you one.

324
00:18:26,331 --> 00:18:29,051
We are the notorious Foxy Pirates!

325
00:18:29,051 --> 00:18:31,291
We want more than just a fight from you!

326
00:18:31,291 --> 00:18:32,731
We want a showdown!

327
00:18:35,451 --> 00:18:36,731
A spirit?

328
00:18:36,731 --> 00:18:37,691
Well, yeah.

329
00:18:37,691 --> 00:18:39,131
What else pops out of a tree?

330
00:18:40,731 --> 00:18:42,491
Hey, can you speak?

331
00:18:44,011 --> 00:18:47,211
You're acting like I don't remember you.

332
00:18:47,211 --> 00:18:48,411
Of course I do.

333
00:18:48,411 --> 00:18:50,251
What have you been up to all these years?

334
00:18:51,051 --> 00:18:51,611
Huh?

335
00:18:51,611 --> 00:18:52,571
You guys know him?

336
00:18:52,571 --> 00:18:54,251
Never seen him.

337
00:18:54,251 --> 00:18:54,891
Same here.

338
00:18:55,691 --> 00:18:58,811
Ah, well, that would explain why I don't remember you then.

339
00:18:58,811 --> 00:18:59,931
Who are you, old man?

340
00:18:59,931 --> 00:19:01,051
And tell us the truth!

341
00:19:01,051 --> 00:19:06,331
If you want my name, it's Tonjit.

342
00:19:06,891 --> 00:19:09,691
But what I intend to give you is my gratitude.

343
00:19:09,691 --> 00:19:12,891
I've been hoping someone would knock me down off those stilts.

344
00:19:12,891 --> 00:19:13,611
Off what?

345
00:19:14,251 --> 00:19:15,051
Uh...

346
00:19:15,051 --> 00:19:18,411
Oh, they are stilts.

347
00:19:18,411 --> 00:19:20,891
We didn't realize because they were so long.

348
00:19:20,891 --> 00:19:23,051
We couldn't even see you.

349
00:19:23,051 --> 00:19:24,811
I'm not surprised.

350
00:19:24,811 --> 00:19:26,891
I couldn't even see the ground up there.

351
00:19:26,891 --> 00:19:31,131
So then, just to get this straight, you're not a bamboo tree spirit.

352
00:19:31,131 --> 00:19:34,651
You're just an old guy whose stilts I happen to think were attacking me.

353
00:19:34,651 --> 00:19:37,291
What were you doing walking around on those stilts anyway?

354
00:19:37,291 --> 00:19:46,411
Well, I've always been a stilt enthusiast, so I decided to break some records and make the world's longest stilts by using the bamboo on this island.

355
00:19:46,411 --> 00:19:50,971
I managed to get on them with a little effort, but then I was too scared to climb down.

356
00:19:50,971 --> 00:19:52,491
That's just plain crazy.

357
00:19:52,491 --> 00:19:54,651
I was up there 10 years.

358
00:19:54,651 --> 00:19:55,851
Really crazy!

359
00:19:55,851 --> 00:19:59,211
Wait, you were up on those stilts for 10 whole years?!

360
00:19:59,211 --> 00:20:04,091
That's right, and to make matters worse, the bamboo kept growing the entire time.

361
00:20:04,091 --> 00:20:07,211
It just kept getting harder and harder to climb down.

362
00:20:08,731 --> 00:20:10,171
So terrifying.

363
00:20:10,171 --> 00:20:12,571
How did you live up there for 10 years?!

364
00:20:12,571 --> 00:20:19,931
Well, most of the trees on this island are just as tall as my stilts, if not taller, so I was well fed from their fruit.

365
00:20:19,931 --> 00:20:22,171
He talks about it like it's no big deal.

366
00:20:22,171 --> 00:20:23,851
10 long years of his life.

367
00:20:23,851 --> 00:20:29,531
And speaking of stuff that's long, how come every living creature on this island is so insanely long?

368
00:20:29,531 --> 00:20:32,891
It might seem crazy to an outsider, but there is a reason.

369
00:20:32,891 --> 00:20:36,731
As I'm sure you've noticed, the island is nothing but grass and trees.

370
00:20:36,731 --> 00:20:40,811
It's dull, so everything grew long out of a longing for excitement.

371
00:20:40,811 --> 00:20:42,731
He can't be serious.

372
00:20:42,731 --> 00:20:43,851
You see that over there?

373
00:20:46,651 --> 00:20:48,571
Platypus.

374
00:20:48,571 --> 00:20:50,651
Ah, you just said it longer!

375
00:20:50,651 --> 00:20:53,371
That one is a dachshund dog.

376
00:20:53,371 --> 00:20:54,891
Whoa, is that the same dog?

377
00:20:56,011 --> 00:20:57,291
It's still passing?

378
00:20:57,291 --> 00:20:57,931
Oh, man!

379
00:20:57,931 --> 00:21:00,811
And there are dangerous animals as well.

380
00:21:00,811 --> 00:21:01,451
See?

381
00:21:01,451 --> 00:21:03,691
Over there is a snow leopard.

382
00:21:03,691 --> 00:21:04,971
I'd steer clear of it.

383
00:21:07,371 --> 00:21:09,931
Why is its head the only thing that's long?!

384
00:21:09,931 --> 00:21:22,411
HBR-

385
00:21:22,411 --> 00:21:24,251
Hmmmm...

386
00:21:24,251 --> 00:21:29,211
A bl-via-via-via...

387
00:21:29,211 --> 00:21:29,871
I'm the captain.

388
00:23:06,218 --> 00:23:08,518
Get out, Luffy! Don't just agree like that!

389
00:23:08,518 --> 00:23:12,518
On the next, One Piece, a Davey back with the Foxy Pirates.

390
00:23:12,518 --> 00:23:15,018
I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

